
EXPERIMENT 1: AGILE SOFTWARE PROJECT LIFECYCLE USING JIRA WITH DEVOPS PIPELINE INTEGRATION

STEP 1: CREATE A JIRA PROJECT

1. Open https://www.atlassian.com/software/jira
2. Sign in or create an account.
3. Create a new project.
4. Project name: ASDD-Demo
5. Choose Scrum.
6. Create the project.

STEP 2: CREATE TASKS IN JIRA

Create the following sprints:

1. Design the application
2. Develop the application
3. Test the application

For a Scrum project:
- Create Sprint 1.
- Add the issues to the sprint.
- Start the sprint.

Move issues across the board:
TO DO → IN PROGRESS → DONE

STEP 3: CREATE A GITHUB REPOSITORY

1. Open https://github.com/
2. Sign in to GitHub.
3. Click New repository.
4. Repository name: asdd-demo
5. Choose Public or Private.
6. Leave Add a README file unchecked.
7. Click Create repository.

STEP 4: CREATE A LOCAL PROJECT FOLDER

Open Command Prompt (CMD) and run:

mkdir asdd-demo
cd asdd-demo
git init

STEP 5: CONFIGURE GIT

Run these commands if Git has not already been configured:

git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "your-email@example.com"

Replace the name and email with your actual details.

STEP 6: CREATE THE APPLICATION

Run:

notepad index.html

Paste the following code into Notepad:

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>ASDD Demo</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome to ASDD Demo</h1>
    <p>Agile project with DevOps integration.</p>
</body>
</html>

Save and close Notepad.

STEP 7: CREATE THE CI WORKFLOW

Create the workflow folders:

mkdir .github
mkdir .github\workflows

Create the workflow file:

notepad .github\workflows\ci.yml

Paste the following YAML code:

name: ASDD CI Pipeline

on:
  push:
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout code
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Verify application
        run: test -f index.html

Save and close Notepad.

STEP 8: ADD AND COMMIT THE FILES

git add .
git commit -m "Create ASDD demo and CI pipeline"

STEP 9: CONNECT TO GITHUB

Replace YOUR_USERNAME with your GitHub username:

git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/asdd-demo.git

STEP 10: PUSH CODE TO GITHUB

git push -u origin main

Sign in or authenticate with GitHub if prompted.

STEP 11: VERIFY THE DEVOPS PIPELINE

1. Open your GitHub repository.
2. Click the Actions tab.
3. Open ASDD CI Pipeline.
4. Confirm that the workflow has completed successfully.
5. A green tick indicates that the workflow passed.

STEP 12: DEMONSTRATE THE AGILE LIFECYCLE

1. Open the ASDD-Demo Jira project.
2. Show the issues on the board.
3. Move an issue from TO DO to IN PROGRESS.
4. Move it to DONE after completion.
5. Show the GitHub repository and successful Actions workflow.
